trong class=3D"style_chapter__grtAe">04</strong><h1>Chat app</h1></header><=
p>In this chapter, we'll tackle the design of a chat app. Chat apps are so =
common that designing one has become a very common question in mobile syste=
m design interviews. Figure 1 showcases some of the most popular chat appli=
cations currently in the market.</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: center=
;"><img alt=3D"Image represents a collection of six popular messaging appli=
cation logos, arranged in two rows and three columns.  The top row features=
, from left to right: a green speech bubble containing a white telephone ic=
on labeled 'Whatsapp,' a light blue speech bubble with a white lightning bo=
lt icon labeled 'Facebook messenger,' and a green square with two overlappi=
