the client sends an 'Upgrade: WebSocket' request to the server via a diagon=
al arrow. The server responds with a '101 Switching Protocols' message, ind=
icated by another diagonal arrow.  Following this protocol switch, bidirect=
ional data transfer occurs between the client's and server's 'WebSocket' co=
mponents, shown by two diagonal arrows labeled 'WebSocket data' in both dir=
ections, indicating continuous, full-duplex communication." loading=3D"lazy=
