new message.  Then, it sends an HTTP request labeled 'NewMessageRequest' (2=
) to the 'Backend.' The 'Backend' processes the message, assigns a new mess=
age ID (3), and replies to the 'Sender' with a 'NewMessageResponse' (4.1). =
The 'Sender' then updates its screen to reflect the message status (5).  Co=
ncurrently, the 'Backend' pushes the new message to the 'Receiver' using a =
WebSockets (WS) event or a push notification (4.2).  The arrows indicate th=
e flow of information and actions between the components.  The numbered ann=
otations describe each step in the process." loading=3D"lazy" width=3D"602"=
