essage Request DAO` components. These DAOs, in turn, feed into `Messages Lo=
cal DataSource`.  `Messages Local DataSource` and `Messages Remote DataSour=
ce` both connect to a central `Messages Repository`.  The `Messages Reposit=
ory` also receives data from `Pending Messages Provider`, which itself rece=
ives data from `Message Request DAO`.  `Messages Remote DataSource` communi=
cates with a `Backend` via `https`.  Finally, a `Messages Scheduler` compon=
ent interacts with `Messages Remote DataSource` and `Pending Messages Provi=
der`, and is controlled by a `Messages Timeout Controller`.  Data flows pri=
marily from the database, through the DAOs and data sources, to the reposit=
ory, then to the scheduler, and finally to the backend.  The `Pending Messa=
ges Provider` acts as a buffer for messages awaiting processing or transmis=
sion." loading=3D"lazy" width=3D"602" height=3D"309" decoding=3D"async" dat=
